#
# Counter-example for gmeow:ResultObjectConflationConstraint's POSITIVE obligation: a
# gmeow:TopologyComputation whose gmeow:producesResult value is a genuine, unrelated
# resource — never conflated with a raw math: object (so the ∀→¬∃ math-namespace arm is
# NOT the violation under test) — but also never asserted rdf:type gmeow:TopologyResult.
# The wrapper type is POSITIVELY required, not merely "permitted and preferred": an
# untyped or wrongly-typed resource does not satisfy gmeow:producesResult's obligation
# any more than a raw math: object does. The computation asserts no global truth, so
# gmeow:AssertedTopologyResultConstraint does not engage. The ∀→(∃∧¬∃) SPARQL constraint
# MUST reject it with shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent, and nothing else — the untyped
# result is the sole violation.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/semantic-topology/tests/> .

ex:computationBad a gmeow:TopologyComputation ;
    gmeow:producesResult ex:untypedResult .        # <-- present, but never typed TopologyResult

ex:untypedResult a gmeow:InformationObject .       # a real resource, just not the wrapper type
